<a name="Intro"></a>
<h1>This example checks that solvers reuse their workspace.</h1>

<h3> In this example, a CG solver preconditioned by multigrid solves a 2D
Poisson problem, while a custom logger counts the allocations of the executor.
The solver is first applied several times, and then regenerated in every step,
as in time stepping, once with the workspace extracted from the previous solver
and once without. After the first apply, the applies should only allocate a
small, constant amount of memory, also after regenerating the solver with the
extracted workspace. The options after the grid size are <tt>profile</tt>,
which additionally prints a nested profile showing where the allocations
happen, and <tt>cudss</tt>, which solves the coarsest level with cuDSS instead
of CG with an SPD ISAI preconditioner on the cuda executor. This requires
Ginkgo's cuDSS extension, and the memory cuDSS allocates itself is not
counted.</h3>
